b0a16cf130ee9a89d1e98f1538b70bcdb2c38ab36b5becae5.webp 200w, /media/d73a1ba896002915820b7f29d875502d3365664b4a24dd045b65f3a03202b9a5.webp 768w, /media/5bcbc88d62e0ab0af71fb30ead3a1334a9c3110af24c92f69a420ddab6d6fe98.webp 1024w, /media/c02b06036b9f09098da3619389f9e5a84c66cb05e43656a0e6905905fb2d1988.webp 1365w, /media/828a8a86e11179f4cf9e4cdd926b304c22bff38501585df6dcbe7fd5ff54450e.webp 750w, /media/8b5a03e5e1972a7c9ca1894b2411cf54da95ad550b5e617dfe006072befa57d2.webp 1140w, /media/e245ad7105cbb6c145817cf41f0f4f69f9b66449fb2dbc52754bbced7c47c5ca.webp 1536w\" /><figcaption>Mike Massaro</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<figure><img loading=\"lazy\" width=\"970\" height=\"647\" src=\"/media/3959aeae9dcd80aefc60535d77bd8726adcce237d2ac0c413428274ee2473e20.webp\" alt=\"Local heroes XO Bikes\" srcset=\"/media/dbd915beaa892736c0482dc1dc02ea2f03fa163650e1c0b2a61329a1a5cc1b67.webp 970w, /media/ba076167b0288a881eaba1cfb9095cc190f708de7dcce5214dc22bcff6ab1c5a.webp 300w, /media/433b444f306725671ccaea639c85e268e9029b66f5afc79f7c56dfc66098ae28.webp 768w, /media/9c7d9dd35447ffc99f2e90b10a16c6d265a9d6d56364c3094c14006a7be4bd3b.webp 750w, /media/6ec2ada642f2d954b5b68113631fc69a469f941e4e2c7beecabc81d9aae7d827.webp 1140w, /media/16ae3531449605036f7a6db7a08aa8f758152bf87db17e97a2b388fb0acc2695.webp 465w, /media/c6bc14b94abc647932da715106afc9381a2e9454ea8f93763568e1bef63a5ead.webp 620w, /media/cb6be868722e633a2720ccb04eb2c37a9be4387c66ac64610066889f7616cb70.webp 350w, /media/fe5bfd66e5408efdf684713ec24b8d177ff38b83ca932b7e5ef0732587a6b57d.webp 1536w\" /><figcaption>Mike Massaro</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2>XO Bikes stories</h2>\n\n\n<div>\n<figure><img loading=\"lazy\" width=\"647\" height=\"970\" src=\"/media/28d3f44ca5b12cdc09fd2b5fed661955c68f2253a41a0601d548097d2c739726.webp\" alt=\"Local heroes XO Bikes\" srcset=\"/media/28d3f44ca5b12cdc09fd2b5fed661955c68f2253a41a0601d548097d2c739726.webp 647w, /media/e6f7d1176cf938f914f2d5c0ec1f0283d158ed5778a51ec349814a07f6835f7e.webp 200w, /media/8463ed9b96415539b22f6233dc79a177b18b246d4dc09ee3aee42cd6f84fdae7.webp 768w, /media/0c049fa8458f9c5d6456ae5955e4fdae889c540284e4e36309e1b2710227e4db.webp 1024w, /media/c91229a102a9e8f1a00a37d7e9146629e2db4c66c2d9838d531799d978d9fce1.webp 1365w, /media/1f8e1dd9731f8bf3766c3d1b953c119c30ebf61a85660093aa26a10ca8deae4f.webp 750w, /media/20cd70171735bffadc3e8094bb7d09d13b481c122c7cdee3f4106ec6f0bed6fc.webp 1140w, /media/0b89fb32b646b152a3b9dfdf4ba04bb9804764241f6f109888dd16299c04cd0f.webp 1536w\" /><figcaption>Assistant trainer Tray was XO’s first graduate and has witnessed the benefits first hand. ‘I’ve seen it change people hugely. It changes their characteristics and their outlook,’ he says.</figcaption><figcaption>Mike Massaro</figcaption></figure></div>\n\n\n<h3>Tray</h3>\n\n\n\n<p><em>Assistant trainer, first graduate, four years</em></p>\n\n\n\n<p>‘I’ve been involved with bikes from when I was 12, mainly BMXs because there was a wooden skatepark right next to my house in Leytonstone. It was maintained by the locals and had a proper community feel. I always thought it might be a career – that or becoming a sponsored rider.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>‘The scheme has trained around 80 people and I’ve seen it change people hugely. It changes their characteristics and their outlook. Some people struggle to engage in a social environment when they arrive, and then by the end they are outgoing and bubbly.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>‘Lots of ex-offenders feel like they don’t have much purpose. Giving guys work to do, where they learn and have that sense of accomplishment, sounds simple but is really helpful.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>‘I also get a lot of pleasure from helping to motivate guys who are earlier on in their journey than I am. I really enjoy what I do and I hope I’m at XO for a long time to come.’</p>\n\n\n<div>\n<figure><img loading=\"lazy\" width=\"647\" height=\"970\" src=\"/media/0a6fcfd93a0b3ef752f44dbde743f6cd7115c7a47a561c15670fbfc7484f7a7b.webp\" alt=\"Local heroes XO Bikes\" srcset=\"/media/0a6fcfd93a0b3ef752f44dbde743f6cd7115c7a47a561c15670fbfc7484f7a7b.webp 647w, /media/3c8ed46f8831c61459e430845199eb206c44615022857484f176dcf5f5aeb64a.webp 200w, /media/a3513048e8e9a9a6fe23da4b309354cd57d0c2ae54bc855749f728d6cf433e7c.webp 768w, /media/d6bd8bb830ec097d535eeccc838c4e1537eb5a8a7f55010d69fcf0524299a3df.webp 1024w, /media/c57b7077a17eab957f257522529f2fd2ff1bdcddeb9097dc3d6fb71ecdd1246a.webp 1365w, /media/2cdeae7e9ab746921821ddef986f62d67686fd995e0acca0eb944eab2d86df4d.webp 750w, /media/38844e392497819aec9c4333eacf3cedcd31df9cafac5f9b73a19ae8132e4fdd.webp 1140w, /media/8bd484d5e730b748e6dc87679f551d39abf4e2f4f8446bdb476cc9928b979618.webp 1536w\" /><figcaption>Jason combines his role at the workshop with outreach work in prisons. ‘It’s good for them to talk to someone who has been in exactly their position,’ he says.</figcaption><figcaption>Mike Massaro</figcaption></figure></div>\n\n\n<h3>Jason</h3>\n\n\n\n<p><em>Assistant manager Lewisham, graduate, three years</em><em></em></p>\n\n\n\n<p>‘I was sitting in my cell in Thameside Prison and I actually saw XO on <em>ITV News</em>. When I lived in the Caribbean I used to ride and work on fixies and racing bikes, so I had a history in bikes, which is why I signed up for the XO course.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>‘Now I do a lot of outreach work, going into prisons and talking with inmates about what we do. It’s good for them to talk to someone who has been in exactly their position and after wasting about 15 years on the street has come out the other side. It gives them some hope.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>‘I’m in a much better position now, contributing to society rather than wasting my time and having a negative impact on those around me. I’m doing more on the charity side and enjoying talking to all kinds of young people – not just those who are caught up in the justice system. I’m a local lad from Woolwich, so hopefully I can share some knowledge that will direct them down the right road.’</p>\n\n\n<div>\n<figure><img loading=\"lazy\" width=\"647\" height=\"970\" src=\"/media/7780d69d422a2abe135d9093838d971c05645c8a4d7391dc411f86d894b00c1a.webp\" alt=\"Local heroes XO Bikes\" srcset=\"/media/7780d69d422a2abe135d9093838d971c05645c8a4d7391dc411f86d894b00c1a.webp 647w, /media/4a036e8b243a2dce9fe747ea63470d76b21c97054111b05da84b6160909a343e.webp 200w, /media/7a71d244f9001089ba27ae5a80c585c5a34b67790ab21d7c9b67e0a6ee2c7bd9.webp 768w, /media/5e8628c67de670a642d78fc910756cc20f7d72ccb597edb725a472604b65a312.webp 1024w, /media/2cf6ca1d05405b1ebc0bd34c4a3a3b0df8a16e16adf751893d81cb3fe248911c.webp 1365w, /media/dd5b5c242b50619e3bb84eb2299f66c80b41259c630792c210e1fb6642658e11.webp 750w, /media/94f0a3730dcb5bd29133ade308575e68f3e5eeeea62e9d0beff917c713ceb516.webp 1140w, /media/6a9d496aac7e9d72662389f4d303adc521700a58539ceec2f7a60d4bf2dfdc0a.webp 1536w\" /><figcaption>XO gives structure and ambition to its graduates. Eugene is working with XO to set up his own bike shop.</figcaption><figcaption>Mike Massaro</figcaption></figure></div>\n\n\n<h3>Eugene</h3>\n\n\n\n<p><em>Graduate and volunteer mechanic at Lewisham, two years </em><em></em></p>\n\n\n\n<p>‘When I first got in touch with XO I didn’t even own a bike. They accepted me onto the programme but I didn’t know a thing. I did six weeks with them, graduated, and have been volunteering for almost two years since.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>‘I was a car mechanic earlier in my life, before I was incarcerated. I started hustling, got into trouble and went to prison in Japan for about ten years, and then came to the UK to complete my sentence. Prison in Japan was a nightmare. As one of the few non-Japanese inmates I couldn’t really talk to anyone, and you have to march everywhere you go.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>‘It’s difficult psychologically too. They wouldn’t use your name, just your prisoner number. Thankfully I had a cell mate who taught me some Japanese but I’ve forgotten most of it now. The guards don’t speak any English so it’s very tricky for a non-native speaker.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>‘In terms of bikes I really like working on derailleurs. It’s challenging but super-rewarding when you get it right. My plan is to set up my own bike shop called Good Spokes. The XO management is keen to support me to help make this happen and I’m on the hunt for a suitable garage as we speak. Hopefully my shop can be a place where more graduates can come and get a job.’</p>\n\n\n<div>\n<figure><img loading=\"lazy\" width=\"647\" height=\"970\" src=\"/media/0e99397ec5ec696a8ceb8d374590586a34188060e81ef15b20c6aa4fd0345eeb.webp\" alt=\"Local heroes XO Bikes\" srcset=\"/media/0e99397ec5ec696a8ceb8d374590586a34188060e81ef15b20c6aa4fd0345eeb.webp 647w, /media/afca9cd7f010efa11541bc71404d834d44964bbc97ba6efebeaf14bbbaf46dad.webp 200w, /media/b1dbd7f5fbe3a59cc2ff37160b56e7f5364be64a6493a6fe833a8b1e739f67d1.webp 768w, /media/ab03c3146cb99c4b3754251aa75f120c0892a27a4b2eff013e175c4589df045d.webp 1024w, /media/e6ea04c9a7c05b30c1d3786d3981957f0d49f7d4e23429130834220a380da9ad.webp 1365w, /media/48ae11098a413639b37e0f0493f2df97233451bbfbeb5cb464c1cd39b72b2eb0.webp 750w, /media/0179a5ecaef88de9452e10ac9ff6c604ed91899b112c991a4dfcc373fb4c1311.webp 1140w, /media/c9dd567409fb7bf54da94d4d62b7064f7bfe5ff14ba1e988c75c5d6e3b70a590.webp 1536w\" /><figcaption>Ross was volunteering for a completely different organisation before finding XO: ‘I went from operating a sewing machine to truing wheels. It was challenging for sure’.</figcaption><figcaption>Mike Massaro</figcaption></figure></div>\n\n\n<h3>Ross</h3>\n\n\n\n<p><em>Mechanic at Blackfriars, recently graduated trainee</em><em></em></p>\n\n\n\n<p>‘I’ve covered a lot of ground in my life to get here. I was born in Scotland but moved to Sydney, Australia, when I was two and spent 40 years there, including some time in prison.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>‘I did a culinary apprenticeship, worked in kitchens, and since I got deported back to the UK I volunteered for a bit at a sewing organisation and then got referred to the XO scheme. I went from operating a sewing machine to truing wheels. It was challenging for sure – I’m not a natural mechanic – but the more I’m challenged the more I enjoy things.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>‘One of the key things the training provides is structure. There’s a tight schedule and you know what your routine is. You’re always meeting new people and keeping your mind busy. That’s good for anyone’s mental health.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>‘Every day is a school day here. Sometimes I’m in the workshop and between my boss and colleagues there are 100 years of bike knowledge between them. It’s like getting cooking lessons off Gordon Ramsay or something.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>‘I honestly don’t know where I would be if it wasn’t for XO – especially in my case when you’re relocated to a new country and you don’t know anyone. XO trained me up and gave me a job. I can’t thank them enough.’</p>\n\n\n<div>\n<figure><a href=\"https://www.cyclist.co.uk/newsletters\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" width=\"970\" height=\"250\" src=\"/media/f3505b92511d2a36ef13f54688cb0ce808010e294fb8c8ea1971d78e4c7f7171.webp\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"/media/f3505b92511d2a36ef13f54688cb0ce808010e294fb8c8ea1971d78e4c7f7171.webp 970w, /media/be42a55005d63c8032bfe3de1330d2f7a16b870775166cd0ced7a9e786855454.webp 300w, /media/c5d133cdbcef4946d0b86f0d28f040ea036748544b9ea2826de7181a281c6bd5.webp 768w, /media/affb43c94f6e1074e36589cc4bd9bd7919354182bbf3c3fbe59db450b317ed22.webp 1536w, /media/e355a8f3da05e50eed9d772a2ed9dc6b912d31b604e154312431d64973c981bb.webp 2048w, /media/f9e1cd1c2f404174a82471c0d8a2ed13646fcb71961b79f6432c86f988bcb1d0.webp 750w, /media/18a0d41dfc48d0253e1e326d64fbb43b9bcdd5d9d3fedde91dca2bf5e9b3742a.webp 1140w\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure></div><p>The post <a href=\"https://www.cyclist.co.uk/in-depth/local-heroes-xo-bikes\">Local heroes: London’s XO Bikes – breaking the chain</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.cyclist.co.uk/\">Cyclist</a>.</p>","author":"Mdonlevy","comments":"https://www.cyclist.co.uk/in-depth/local-heroes-xo-bikes#respond","siteTitle":"Cyclist.co.uk","siteHash":"561486e7070fa5351de9318ad0fa26c2a39332acba5fc7c7d1694a01d53d431e","entryHash":"5930019ae846198ed412cb29cded5f167af2fd4d725579d5acbc3773b5a91f35","category":"Cycling"}